### 4.5 Security & Firestore Rules

| ID      | Title                               | Priority | Pre-condition             | Steps | Expected Result |
|---------|--------------------------------------|----------|---------------------------|-------|-----------------|
| SEC-01  | Free Tier – Material Data Leak       | Critical | Free student logged in    | 1. Use browser DevTools / Firestore API to read a material where `isFreePreview = false`. | **Permission denied** (or data filtered by app logic). |
| SEC-02  | Paid Tier – Material Read            | Critical | Paid student logged in    | 1. Read the same restricted material via API. | Read **allowed**. |
| SEC-03  | Cross-Teacher Write Prevention       | Critical | Teacher A logged in       | 1. Attempt to update a course owned by Teacher B via REST/Console. | Firestore returns **permission-denied**. |
| SEC-04  | Unauthenticated Course Write         | Critical | Not logged in             | 1. Try to create a course via API. | Request **rejected**. |
| SEC-05  | Student Cannot Write Courses         | High     | Student logged in         | 1. Try to create/update a course via API. | **Permission denied** (create may succeed per current rules — flag for review). |
| SEC-06  | Questions – Only Owner Can Delete    | High     | Student A logged in       | 1. Try to delete a question posted by Student B. | **Permission denied**. |
| SEC-07  | Admin Can Manage Any User            | High     | Admin logged in           | 1. Read/write another user's document. | Allowed. |
| SEC-08  | User Cannot Read Other User Docs     | High     | Student A logged in       | 1. Try to read Student B's user document. | **Permission denied**. |

> **⚠ Note (SEC-05):** Current `firestore.rules` allows any authenticated user to `create` a course. This should be restricted to users with `role: "teacher"` or `role: "admin"`. **Flag as a potential defect.**

